  "question": "For $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&1&3\\\\0&4&-1\\\\5&2&1\\end{bmatrix}$, calculate the cofactors $A_{11}$, $A_{21}$ and $A_{31}$. Hence, evaluate $|A|$ by expanding along the first column.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "<b>First cofactor</b><br>$$A_{11}=\\begin{vmatrix}4&-1\\\\2&1\\end{vmatrix}=4+2=6$$<br><b>Second cofactor</b><br>$$A_{21}=-\\begin{vmatrix}1&3\\\\2&1\\end{vmatrix}=-(1-6)=5$$<br><b>Third cofactor</b><br>$$A_{31}=\\begin{vmatrix}1&3\\\\4&-1\\end{vmatrix}=-1-12=-13$$<br><b>Expansion along the first column</b><br>Therefore, $$|A|=2(6)+0(5)+5(-13)=12-65=-53$$",
